#@@ md
# INF2006 Big Data Project — Spark pipeline, model and analytics (AWS EMR)

**Kernel:** PySpark (JupyterHub on EMR `emr-7.10.0`). **Run it with:** `Kernel → Restart & Run All` (or run the cells top to bottom).
**Before this notebook** the two shell stages must already have run on the primary node (they use Hadoop Streaming and Hive, which need the cluster's command line):

| Stage | Engine | Script (relative path in the ZIP) | Output used here |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | S3 → HDFS (DistCp) | `scripts/stage1_stage_to_hdfs.sh` | `/raw/prices/<version>/`, `/raw/gdelt/<version>/` |
| 2 | Hadoop Streaming + Hive on Tez | `scripts/stage2_streaming_and_hive.sh` | Hive database `inf2006` (`prices_typed`, `gdelt_daily_typed`, …) |
| 3–5 | **PySpark / Spark ML (this notebook)** | `notebooks/inf2006_pipeline.ipynb` | cleaned/rejected data, splits, models, analytics, timings |

`scripts/emr_run_all.sh` runs stages 1–2 for you in one command. Full step-by-step guide: `docs/RUN_ON_EMR.md` (this is Appendix A).

| Section | Brief reference |
|---|---|
| 0 Setup, environment, helper functions | Cloud resource constraints, reproducibility |
| 1 Corpus checks (Task 1) | Task 1.2 |
| 2 Cleaning, features, chronological splits (Task 2) | Task 2.1–2.3 |
| 3 Models: weekly direction + high-volatility weeks (Task 3) | Task 3.1–3.3 |
| 4 Analytics (Task 4) | Task 4.1–4.3 |
| 5 Performance, memory, repetitions (Section 6 of the report) | Cloud resource constraints |
| 6 Saved-model reload in a fresh session | Task 3.3 |
| 7 Verification record | Submission requirements |

> **Honesty rule used throughout:** every check prints *expected* and *actual*; failed checks are reported, never hidden.

